# Copy to .env and fill in. .env is gitignored.
#
# ⚑ YOU ALMOST CERTAINLY WANT THE ROOT .env INSTEAD. The shared connection at the repo root is read
# by every kit, including the ones that do not exist yet -- set it once there and this file is not
# needed. A kit-local .env is an OVERRIDE, merged key by key, and it is for pointing THIS kit at a
# different model: a tier comparison, a local server, a provider you are trying out.
#
# THEIR PROVIDER, NOT OURS. A kit that hardcodes one vendor is broken for most of the people who
# fork it. PROVIDER picks the adapter, MODEL picks the model behind it.
#
# ⚑ YOU DO NOT NEED A KEY TO SEE THIS KIT WORK, AND ON THIS ONE THE FREE HALF IS THE ARGUMENT.
# The corpus is generated from a fixed seed and the floor is pure code:
#
#     python3 tools/build_corpus.py     # the corpus, byte-identical every rebuild
#     python3 -m evals.check_labels     # every tool exists, every sequence is runnable
#     python3 -m evals.baseline         # a WORKING keyword router over 4 call budgets, 0 calls
#     python3 -m evals.escalate         # router-then-model policies, re-scored. Still 0 calls
#
# A key is needed only to re-run the model over the 120 requests -- `python3 -m evals.run`. The
# recorded run is already committed in results/, so every number in the README is readable offline.
#
# ⚠︎ IF THIS KIT SITS INSIDE THE KITS REPO, IT ALREADY INHERITS THE ROOT .env AND THEREFORE A LIVE
# KEY. "I have not configured anything yet" is not the same as "nothing can spend". Run
# `python3 -m evals.run --dry-run` before touching anything that calls out.
#
# ⚠︎ AND ON THIS KIT THE MODEL CHOOSES THE BILL. A request averaged 1.75 calls on the recorded run,
# so 120 requests is not 120 calls. src/loop.py::MAX_STEPS is the ceiling that bounds it.

PROVIDER=openai-compatible
BASE_URL=https://api.openai.com/v1
API_KEY=
MODEL=

# No EMBED_MODEL: nothing is embedded. The six policy notes are grepped and the database is
# queried directly, which is why this kit has no index and no build step.
